@echo off
cd /d "C:\Users\SubratoBiswas\trinamix-conversion-workbench"
echo Cleaning any git locks...
del /f /q ".git\index.lock" 2>nul
del /f /q ".git\HEAD.lock" 2>nul
echo Dropping tracked bytecode...
git rm -r --cached --ignore-unmatch backend/app/__pycache__ backend/app/services/__pycache__ backend/app/parsers/__pycache__
echo Staging...
git add -A
echo Committing (no-op if clean)...
git commit -m "Customer generate: prune unmapped source columns to cut peak memory. Read the real console error on the user's frontend: it reports a CORS block (No Access-Control-Allow-Origin) + net::ERR_FAILED, but backend CORS is allow_origins=['*'] - so it is NOT a real CORS misconfig. That message is how the browser surfaces a request that DIED at Render's gateway (a 502): the gateway's error response carries no CORS headers. Fast GETs succeed; the heavy Customer generate 502s and shows up as 'CORS'. Confirms the diagnosis - generate is exceeding the free-tier's memory/timeout. Biggest remaining hog: build_converted_dataframe parsed the ENTIRE 5599x234 source, but the transform only needs the ~64 mapped columns. Now it drops every non-mapped source column right after load (guarded, only when there's real excess), bounding peak memory to the mapped slice. Consistent with the transform, which already only reads mapped columns for row context. If this still 502s on the 512MB free tier, the durable fix is background generation (return immediately, poll for the artifact) so a heavy run can't hit the ~100s gateway timeout."
echo Pushing...
git push origin main
echo.
echo ====== DONE - Press any key to close ======
pause
